# Desktop Application (Not a Website)

This project is a **Windows Desktop Application** built with Electron. It is NOT a website, web app, or anything that requires a browser to run.

## Core constraints

- The output is a `.exe` Windows installer (NSIS) via electron-builder
- Users install it like any normal Windows program (Start Menu, desktop shortcut)
- It runs fully offline on the local PC — no web server, no hosting, no cloud
- The user launches it from their desktop or Start Menu, not from a browser URL
- Every PC runs its own copy of the app, all sharing one SQLite database file over the network

## What NOT to do

- Do NOT suggest or build a web server (Express, Fastify, etc.) as a runtime dependency
- Do NOT suggest hosting the app on a web domain or cloud platform
- Do NOT write code that requires a browser to open a URL to use the app
- Do NOT suggest Progressive Web App (PWA) as a delivery mechanism
- Do NOT create REST/HTTP APIs for the frontend to consume
- Do NOT use `create-react-app`, `next dev`, `vite dev`, or any dev-server-only workflow as the delivery mechanism

## All IPC communication must use Electron's `ipcMain.handle` / `ipcRenderer.invoke`

- The React renderer calls `window.tracker.*` methods
- These are wired through Electron's preload script and `contextBridge`
- All data access goes through the main process (Node.js side) which talks directly to SQLite via `better-sqlite3`

## Target OS

- Primary: Windows 10/11 (x64)
- No Linux or macOS support required (unless explicitly requested later)
